Enumerating all games is intractable.

Enumerating all positions becomes feasible and
quite simple for computers once you are in the
late endgame, with very few pieces on the board.
For such purposes you can just build lookup tables
showing the optimal move for any given position.

This analysis has in fact been used to show that
the 50 move rule is insufficient in certain positions.
Several specific endgames have been extended to
75 moves.  There is also a record requiring 517
moves (assuming optimal play) for a position with
queen and knight against rook, bishop and knight.
In practice, defense is harder and the positions
rarely take so long.

